            <ArticleTitle>[Assisted circulation. The effect of cardio-synchronous peripheral arterio-arterial counterpulsation on perfusion and metabolism in the area of acute transmural myocardial ischemia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>160-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>After establishing a model of ischemia, perfusion in the ischemic area was considerably disturbed. Examination by means of 133xenon-clearance after intramyocardiac injection showed strongly delayed flowing-off compared with controls. Counterpulsation accelerates the flowing-off (perfusion). Untreated control animals reveal after inducing the model ischemia a crucial decrease of ATP concentration and an excessive increase of lactate concentration in the ischemic area. Counterpulsation may inhibit further decrease of ATP in the ischemic area.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
